title: Forced Safe Mode Boot Configuration
id: 84b3791e-f136-497c-9266-90942c4f7bea
status: experimental
description: Detects bcdedit configuring the system to boot into Safe Mode (safeboot), a technique ransomware uses to run encryption with most security tools disabled, often paired with a service registered to start in Safe Mode.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1562/009/
logsource:
  product: windows
  category: process_creation
detection:
  selection:
    Image|endswith: '\\bcdedit.exe'
    CommandLine|contains: 'safeboot'
  condition: selection
fields:
  - CommandLine
  - Image
  - ParentImage
falsepositives:
  - Administrators troubleshooting in Safe Mode
level: high
tags:
  - attack.defense_evasion
  - attack.t1562.009
